 is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" Swift package shipped alongside the sample, and it does most of the work. Intercepting ","type":"text"},{"code":"navigator.credentials.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" means giving up the platform’s built-in WebAuthn sheets (tap prompt, PIN entry, errors, success) — ","type":"text"},{"code":"FidoUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" replaces them end-to-end with a complete ceremony UI: connect \/ touch, PIN entry with retry counters, PIN change, first-time PIN setup, forced PIN-change recovery, fingerprint enrollment, credential picker, and error \/ success results. The host app stays a thin shell.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Beyond the panels, it owns the moving parts that you’d otherwise re-implement per app:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Transport selection.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" On iOS it tries wired (USB-C \/ Lightning) first and falls back to NFC; on macOS it uses HID FIDO. Connections are polled and reused across a ceremony.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ceremony serialization."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Concurrent calls on the same "},{"code":"FidoUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance are queued so they don’t fight over the alert window, transport, or shared panel state.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Cancellation.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" A single ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cancel()"},{"text":" call (used by the WebView coordinator on dismiss \/ new message) tears down the active transport and dismisses any visible panel.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The host code only needs to construct one ","type":"text"},{"type":